# 🫀 AI Healthcare Lab 1 — Heart Failure Data Analysis & Preprocessing

## 📌 Overview

This project performs exploratory data analysis (EDA), data cleaning, missing-value handling, feature engineering, and numerical feature scaling on a clinical heart-failure dataset.

The objective is to prepare healthcare data for further machine-learning applications by identifying data-quality issues, understanding feature distributions, creating meaningful derived features, and transforming numerical variables into a suitable scale.

---

## 🎯 Objectives

The main objectives of this laboratory are:

- Load and inspect the heart-failure dataset.
- Understand the structure and characteristics of the data.
- Identify missing values.
- Handle missing numerical and categorical values.
- Perform exploratory data analysis.
- Visualize feature distributions and potential outliers.
- Create new features through feature engineering.
- Develop a patient risk score.
- Normalize numerical features using Min-Max scaling.
- Compare the dataset before and after preprocessing.

---

## 📊 Dataset

The project uses a clinical heart-failure dataset containing **299 patient records and 13 variables**.

### Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| `age` | Age of the patient |
| `anaemia` | Whether the patient has anaemia |
| `creatinine_phosphokinase` | Level of creatinine phosphokinase |
| `diabetes` | Whether the patient has diabetes |
| `ejection_fraction` | Percentage of blood leaving the heart during contraction |
| `high_blood_pressure` | Whether the patient has high blood pressure |
| `platelets` | Platelet count |
| `serum_creatinine` | Serum creatinine level |
| `serum_sodium` | Serum sodium level |
| `sex` | Patient sex |
| `smoking` | Whether the patient smokes |
| `time` | Follow-up period |
| `DEATH_EVENT` | Target variable indicating a death event |

